<article class="env-corollary" id="8F9FE8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8F9FE8">Corollary <span data-tag="8F9FE8">5.2.8.18</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category equipped with a factorization system $(S_ L, S_ R)$, and let $K$ be an arbitrary simplicial set. Then the $\infty $-category $\Fun (K, \calC )$ admits a factorization system $(S_ L^{K}, S_ R^{K})$, where $S_{L}^{K}$ denotes the collection of all morphisms $f$ in $\Fun (K, \calC )$ such that $f(v) \in S_ L$ for each vertex $v$ of $K$, and $S_{R}^{K}$ is defined likewise. </p>
